    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "A throat clears pointedly beside me. “Hello, Friend.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1908
        },
        {
          "text": "Reapers are expressly forbidden from forming attachments with their assigned souls. They must be dispassionate about the",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3414
        },
        {
          "text": "As far as I know, though, this rule never has been broken. Humans recoil from us. We cannot experience physical connecti",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3637
        },
        {
          "text": "It was for me as well—until now",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3812
        }
      ],
      "words": 60
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "How does Lucy McKenzie cope with uncertainty? Please respond in no more than six sentences",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4401
        },
        {
          "text": "Lucy McKenzie has had to cope with an unfair amount of uncertainty in her too-short life. Not all of her coping mechanis",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4608
        },
        {
          "text": "Lucy McKenzie has cripplingly low self-esteem for someone as kind, clever, and funny as she is",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5015
        }
      ],
      "words": 69
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“Consider this a warning, Friend. You will maintain professional boundaries with your assigned souls at all times.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5649
        },
        {
          "text": "But holding Lucy, kissing her, awoke something in me that had been dormant so long I’d forgotten what longing was",
